{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1315637744/14/prompt.md && printf '\\\\n---DES---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1315637744/14/des.md\"","aggregated_output":"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8b9c3697\" lines=\"9-23\">\n<description>\nInsert red components into interior sockets of large structures, leaving a black trail.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common. Large non-bg, non-red structures with interior cavities.\n- Red components outside structures.\n\nRule:\n- Interior sockets: bg cells inside a structure's bbox, adjacent to structure pixels.\n- For each structure, find the direction where rays from sockets hit a red component.\n- Slide that component into the socket; paint traversed cells black.\n- Unmatched reds vanish.\n\nKey insight: Docking direction is inferred by ray-casting from interior sockets to the nearest red component.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"60d73be6\" lines=\"22-39\">\n<description>\nComplete the sparse colored marker pattern by reflecting it across a full-row/full-column cross.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has a dominant background and one non-background cross color that\nfills exactly one complete row and one complete column. All other foreground\npixels are sparse markers away from that cross.\n\nRule\nKeep the input unchanged, and for each marker pixel copy its color to the\npositions obtained by reflecting it across the cross row, across the cross\ncolumn, and across both axes. Reflected positions outside the grid are\nclipped.\n\nKey insight\nThe full cross is not a copied object; it is the pair of mirror axes for\ncompleting the quadrant pattern.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"22806e14\" lines=\"23-37\">\n<description>\nMark the center of each odd-sized solid square with the plus marker color, erasing the marker only when it is outside the marked-center field.\n\nInput structure:\n- The dominant color is background.\n- Exactly two foreground colors are present: one unique 3x3 plus marker and one color forming separated solid square objects.\n\nRule:\n- For every non-marker 4-connected object, assert it is a solid square.\n- If the square side length is odd, recolor its center pixel to the plus marker color; even-sided squares stay unchanged.\n- Preserve the plus marker when its center lies inside the bounding box of the odd-square centers; otherwise erase it to background.\n\nKey insight:\n- Odd-sided solid squares have a single visible center pixel, and the plus supplies the color used to identify those centers.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e45ef808\" lines=\"31-46\">\n<description>\nMark the shallowest and deepest columns of a solid terrain boundary with vertical colored guide lines.\n\nInput structure:\n- The first row is a solid empty separator.\n- Below it, each column consists of upper fill cells followed by a contiguous suffix of terrain cells.\n- The bottom row is all terrain, so every column has a well-defined first terrain row.\n\nRule:\n- Find the column whose first terrain row is latest; it is unique and its upper fill run becomes maroon.\n- Find the rightmost column whose first terrain row is earliest; its upper fill run becomes yellow.\n- Preserve the empty separator, terrain cells, and all other upper fill cells.\n\nKey insight:\n- The task is a column-height summary of the terrain profile: color the deepest upper run and the highest terrain peak.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2b9ef948\" lines=\"51-65\">\n<description>\nMove the yellow 3x3 frame by the displacement encoded by the gray path, then draw its diagonal yellow corner rays.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is black.\n- One 3x3 yellow frame has a non-yellow control-color center.\n- A second control-color pixel is connected through gray path pixels to a lone yellow endpoint.\n\nRule:\n- Use the vector from the second control-color pixel to the lone yellow endpoint as the frame's translation.\n- Fill the whole output with the control color.\n- Draw the translated yellow frame and extend yellow diagonal rays outward from its four corners to the grid edge.\n\nKey insight: The gray path's turns are irrelevant; its two colored endpoints encode the net displacement to apply to the frame.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"247ef758\" lines=\"35-46\">\n<description>\nMove colored sprites from the left strip into a framed area at marker-defined targets.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg background; rectangular frame on right with colored markers on its edges; sprites in a narrow left strip separated by a constant-color divider column.\n\nRule:\n- For each color, target rows/cols are where both opposite frame edges share that color. Targets are the Cartesian product.\n- Erase each sprite from the left and stamp it centered at every target. Higher sprites cover lower ones.\n\nKey insight: One sprite replicates to a grid of row × column marker intersections.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"37ce87bb\" lines=\"33-47\">\n<description>\nCompute a grey result bar by adding teal bar heights and subtracting red bar heights.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a dominant background and several bottom-aligned one-cell-wide vertical bars.\n- Teal bars are positive operands; red bars are negative operands.\n- The penultimate column is an empty result slot.\n\nRule\n- Keep every input bar unchanged.\n- Compute result height = total teal bar height - total red bar height.\n- Paint that many bottom cells of the penultimate column grey.\n\nKey insight\n- The bars encode arithmetic by height, with color providing the sign.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"abc82100\" lines=\"70-86\">\n<description>\nUse local source-target-pattern examples to replace matching source pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- Black background with isolated colored pixels and teal (8) pattern components.\n- A rule example is a 4-neighbor colored pair source->target whose continued\n  direction reaches an anchor touching a teal pattern component.\n\nRule:\n- For each rule example, copy that teal component onto every other pixel of\n  source.color, recoloring the copied component to target.color.\n- Translation maps the rule anchor onto the source pixel being replaced.\n- Remove teal components and all pixels used by rule examples.\n\nKey insight: The two adjacent colored pixels define the color substitution and\nthe anchor point; the nearby teal component is the stencil that gets recolored.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"342ae2ed\" lines=\"34-49\">\n<description>\nDraw the missing diagonal connector segment between each pair of same-color rectangular objects.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has one dominant background color.\n- Every foreground color appears as exactly two separated solid rectangular 4-connected objects.\n- The two rectangles of each color are diagonally offset with facing corners on a 45-degree line.\n\nRule:\n- Keep all existing rectangles unchanged.\n- For each foreground color, connect the lower facing corner of the upper rectangle to the upper facing corner of the lower rectangle.\n- Paint only the intervening background pixels on that diagonal, excluding the two endpoint pixels already in the rectangles.\n\nKey insight:\n- Same-color rectangles define the endpoints; the output completes the open diagonal between their nearest facing corners.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"182e5d0f\" lines=\"89-103\">\n<description>\nMove each gray marker along its green path until it reaches the cell next to a black-green-black gate, erasing the path behind it.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Foreground components are made from a path color, a paired gate-end color, and single marker pixels.\n- A gate is a straight end-center-end motif whose center has the path color and whose two ends share the gate-end color.\n\nRule:\n- In every 4-connected foreground component with exactly one marker and one gate, erase the marker and all path-color pixels except the gate center.\n- Place the marker on the unique path-color pixel adjacent to the gate center but not between the two gate ends.\n- Components without both a marker and a gate stay unchanged.\n\nKey insight: The black-green-black motif marks the stopping gate; the gray marker consumes the connected green path until it rests on the path cell immediately beside that gate.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d255d7a7\" lines=\"99-114\">\n<description>\nMove the patterned edge band to the opposite edge along every row or column whose band slice contains the trail color.\n\nInput structure\n- The dominant color is the background.\n- The two foreground colors are a frequent trail color and a rarer marker color.\n- All marker pixels lie nearest to one grid edge, and that edge contains trail-color runs that define the source-band thickness.\n\nRule\n- Choose the source edge identified by the marker pixels.\n- A row or column perpendicular to that edge moves if its source-band slice contains the trail color.\n- Copy that slice unchanged to the opposite edge, erase the remaining trail cells to background, and keep marker-only lines fixed.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker color identifies the active edge, while the trail color identifies which parallel rows or columns carry an edge-band slice across the grid.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"7ec998c9\" lines=\"14-28\">\n<description>\nDraw a blue folded corner-to-corner route through the lone marker's column.\n\nInput structure:\n- A rectangular grid filled with one background color.\n- Exactly one non-background marker pixel; blue is absent from the input.\n\n---DES---\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据封闭区域内部的孔洞数量，从颜色图例条中选取对应颜色，对该区域进行重新填充。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（black）。\n  - 网格中存在若干由同一种非背景颜色（如 grey）绘制的封闭不规则形状，每个形状的边界宽度为 1 像素，内部可能包含 0 到若干个黑色孔洞（即被边界完全包围但未被填充的黑色连通区域）。\n  - 网格的最底部一行或最右侧一列存在一个颜色图例条：图例条由若干连续的单色段组成，每段长度为 1 像素，从左到右（或从上到下）依次排列不同的颜色，分别对应孔洞数 0、1、2、3……例如第一个颜色对应 0 个孔洞，第二个颜色对应 1 个孔洞，以此类推。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 保留所有封闭形状的边界像素不变。\n  - 对每个封闭形状，数出其内部包含多少个独立的黑色孔洞（4-连通区域）。\n  - 用孔洞数作为索引，在颜色图例条中查找对应颜色（索引从 0 开始）。\n  - 将该封闭形状内部所有非孔洞的黑色像素填充为查找到的颜色；孔洞保持黑色。\n  - 输出中移除颜色图例条（将其恢复为背景色）。\n\n- `Key insight`：封闭形状本身的颜色和大小无关紧要，决定填充颜色的是每个形状内部孔洞的数量，而图例条提供了从数量到颜色的映射关系。解题者需要先识别图例条的位置和含义，再对每个形状计数孔洞并完成颜色匹配。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将散落的单色碎片按颜色匹配到对应的矩形框架中，碎片进入框架后需按框架开口方向的反方向平移至紧靠对边。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（black）。\n  - 网格中存在若干个不同颜色的矩形框架（空心矩形），每个框架恰好在一条边上有一个连续的缺口（缺口宽度大于 1 像素）。框架的颜色各不相同。\n  - 网格中另有若干个与框架颜色一一对应的小型实心碎片（4-连通的不规则形状），每个碎片的颜色与某个框架颜色相同，且碎片的形状恰好能嵌入对应框架的缺口。\n  - 碎片位于其对应框架的外部，且位于缺口方向的一侧。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：识别每个碎片与框架的颜色匹配关系，以及框架缺口所在的边（上、下、左、右）。\n  - 第二步：将碎片沿垂直于缺口边的方向滑入框架内部，滑动方向为从缺口侧朝向对边，碎片一直滑动直到碰到框架的对边内壁为止。\n  - 第三步：碎片到达最终位置后，将缺口处原本缺失的框架边界像素补全（用框架颜色填充），使框架变为完整的封闭矩形。\n  - 框架外部原碎片位置恢复为背景色。\n\n- `Key insight`：碎片不是直接填入缺口位置，而是穿过缺口后继续滑动到框架的对边。解题者需要识别出缺口方向决定了碎片的运动方向，而终点是对边而非缺口本身，这一\"穿透\"机制是非显然的核心规律。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：每个彩色对象根据其所在象限确定旋转角度，旋转后按面积从大到小的顺序依次叠加绘制到网格中心。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（black）。\n  - 网格中有一条由 grey 颜色绘制的完整水平线和一条完整垂直线，将网格分为四个象限。\n  - 四个象限中各自分布着一个或多个不同颜色的实心 4-连通对象，每个对象完全位于某一个象限内。\n  - 同一种颜色只出现一次。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 以灰色十字线的交叉点为网格中心。\n  - 每个对象根据其所在象限被赋予一个旋转角度：右上象限 = 0°，左上象限 = 顺时针 90°，左下象限 = 顺时针 180°，右下象限 = 顺时针 270°。\n  - 将每个对象按其对应角度进行旋转。\n  - 所有旋转后的对象按面积从大到小排序，依次以网格中心为锚点（对象的边界框中心对齐到网格中心）进行叠加绘制，面积小的对象后画因此在最上层。\n  - 灰色十字线在输出中被移除（恢复为背景色）。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要发现两层独立的规律——第一层是象限位置与旋转角度的映射关系（并非对称翻转，而是累进旋转），第二层是叠加顺序由面积决定（大的先画、小的覆盖）。两层规律都需要从样例中分别归纳。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：沿每个箭头指向的方向发射与箭头等长的射线，射线颜色由箭头所指向的目标对象的颜色决定。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（black）。\n  - 网格中存在若干个由不同颜色绘制的小型实心矩形对象（宽高均 ≥ 2）。\n  - 网格中还存在若干个由 grey 颜色绘制的箭头。每个箭头由一条直线段（水平或垂直，长度 ≥ 2 像素）和一个位于线段一端的单像素三角尖端组成：尖端位于线段延伸方向的前方，偏离线段主轴一个像素（例如，一个向右的水平箭头，其尖端在线段最右端像素的右上方或右下方，形成一个\">\"形末端）。箭头的\"长度\"定义为线段部分的像素数（不含尖端）。\n  - 每个箭头的尖端方向上一定存在一个矩形对象（沿箭头方向做射线能最先命中该对象）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：对每个箭头，确定其指向方向（由尖端决定）和长度（线段像素数）。\n  - 第二步：沿箭头方向做射线投射，找到最先命中的矩形对象，记录该对象的颜色。\n  - 第三步：从箭头尖端开始，沿箭头方向继续延伸一条新射线，射线长度等于箭头的线段长度，射线颜色为第二步中获取的目标对象颜色。\n  - 保留所有原始对象和箭头不变，仅添加新的射线像素。射线像素不覆盖已有非背景像素。\n\n- `Key insight`：射线的长度编码在箭头自身的几何属性中（线段长度），而射线的颜色编码在箭头与环境的空间关系中（指向哪个对象）。解题者需要分别从两个不同来源推断同一条射线的两个属性，这构成了两层独立的归纳。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在分格棋盘中，每个格子的填充颜色由该格子所在行的行标记颜色和所在列的列标记颜色共同决定：取两种标记颜色在色带图例中的位置之和，对色带长度取循环后查找对应颜色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（black）。\n  - 网格被 grey 线条分割为若干等大的方格（类似棋盘），形成 R 行 × C 列的方格阵列。\n  - 方格阵列的左侧有一列标记像素，每行一个，颜色各异，作为该行的\"行标记\"。\n  - 方格阵列的上方有一行标记像素，每列一个，颜色各异，作为该列的\"列标记\"。\n  - 网格的某个角落（如左上角）有一条由若干不同颜色像素排成的短色带，作为颜色图例，长度为 L（L ≤ 6）。色带中每个像素位置编号从 0 到 L-1。\n  - 行标记和列标记使用的颜色均来自色带中出现的颜色。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对色带中的每种颜色赋予位置编号（从 0 开始）。\n  - 对于方格阵列中第 i 行、第 j 列的格子：找到第 i 行的行标记颜色在色带中的位置编号 a，找到第 j 列的列标记颜色在色带中的位置编号 b，计算 (a + b)，若超过 L-1 则从头循环（即 (a + b) mod L，但此处循环是视觉上色带首尾相接的自然循环），取色带中对应位置的颜色填充该格子。\n  - 输出中保留 grey 分格线、行列标记和色带。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要发现三层结构——第一层是识别色带作为颜色顺序的图例，第二层是发现行标记和列标记各自映射到色带中的位置编号，第三层是发现格子颜色由两个编号之和在色带上循环查找得到。单看行或列都无法解释格子颜色的变化规律，必须同时考虑行列的联合作用。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：每对同色像素之间的连线段作为\"刀\"，切割它所穿过的所有多色对象，被切割的部分沿垂直于刀的方向分离一个像素的间距。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（black）。\n  - 网格中存在若干个由不同颜色绘制的实心矩形对象（每种颜色一个矩形）。\n  - 网格中还存在若干对 red 像素（red 不用于矩形），每对 red 像素在同一行或同一列上对齐，且两个像素之间有一定距离。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每对同行/同列的 red 像素，在它们之间画一条虚拟的直线段（水平或垂直），这条线段即为\"切割线\"。\n  - 切割线穿过的每个矩形被沿切割线分成两部分。\n  - 分割后，矩形的两个部分沿垂直于切割线的方向各自向外平移 1 个像素（即两部分之间形成 2 像素宽的间隙，间隙中心在原切割线位置）。\n  - 如果一个矩形被多条切割线穿过，则依次应用所有切割（先水平后垂直），每次切割都会将已有碎片进一步分裂和位移。\n  - 输出中移除所有 red 像素。\n\n- `Key insight`：red 像素对定义了隐形的切割线，而不是路径或连接。解题者需要先识别出 red 像素的配对关系和连线含义，再理解切割后的分离方向（垂直于切割线而非沿着切割线），最后还要处理多刀叠加切割的顺序效应。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：网格中的每个\"种子\"像素按照其相邻的方向标记所指示的方向，生长出与种子颜色相同的线段，线段长度等于种子所在封闭房间的面积。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（black）。\n  - 网格中存在由 grey 像素绘制的墙壁，墙壁将网格划分为若干个封闭的矩形房间（每个房间的内部为黑色）。\n  - 每个房间内部恰好有一个非黑、非灰的彩色\"种子\"像素。\n  - 每个种子像素恰好有一个 4-邻接的 azure 像素位于同一房间内，该 azure 像素位于种子像素的上、下、左或右方，指示生长方向（azure 在种子的哪一侧，种子就朝那个方向生长）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个房间，计算房间内部的面积（黑色像素 + 种子像素 + azure 像素的总数）。\n  - 种子像素从自身位置开始，朝 azure 标记所指示的方向，穿过墙壁延伸到房间外部，画出一条与种子颜色相同的直线段。\n  - 线段长度（像素数，不含种子本身）等于该房间的内部面积。\n  - 线段可以覆盖墙壁像素和其他房间的内容，但不覆盖其他种子像素。\n  - 输出中移除所有 azure 标记像素（恢复为背景色），保留墙壁和种子。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先理解 azure 像素不是装饰而是方向指针，再发现线段长度由房间面积决定——而房间面积是视觉上可数但不显然与线段长度关联的量。方向来自局部（邻接标记），长度来自全局（房间尺寸），两者融合构成核心双层推理。\n</new_puzzle>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"已提取到参考实现的共同做法：`main()` 先做结构断言并直接按题意求解，`generate_input()` 通过“候选生成 + 约束验证 + 失败重试”避免退化样例。我会按这个模式实现本题，并把多刀顺序、红点配对唯一性、以及切割后不越界作为生成器的核心约束。\n\n计划：\n1. 明确几何规则并选定内部表示：把每个矩形视为若干同色像素，按“先水平后垂直”对像素集合做切割与平移。\n2. 设计稳健的红点配对识别：仅允许每个 red 像素在同一行或同一列上各命中唯一一个 red 对端，避免歧义。\n3. 设计生成器：随机网格、随机矩形、随机水平/垂直刀数量；只保留确实穿过至少一个矩形且最终输出不越界的方案，并控制对象间距保证视觉清晰。\n4. 写入目标文件后运行你指定的 100 次变体自检和 `py_compile`，若失败就回头修约束或解法。\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef apply(coords, hcuts, vcuts):\n    pts=[tuple(p) for p in coords]\n    for r in sorted(hcuts):\n        new=[]\n        for pr,pc in pts:\n            if pr < r:\n                new.append((pr-1,pc))\n            elif pr > r:\n                new.append((pr+1,pc))\n        pts=new\n    for c in sorted(vcuts):\n        new=[]\n        for pr,pc in pts:\n            if pc < c:\n                new.append((pr,pc-1))\n            elif pc > c:\n                new.append((pr,pc+1))\n        pts=new\n    return sorted(pts)\n\ncoords=[(r,c) for r in range(2,6) for c in range(2,7)]\nprint('orig', min(r for r,c in coords),max(r for r,c in coords),min(c for r,c in coords),max(c for r,c in coords))\nprint(apply(coords,[3],[4])[:20], len(apply(coords,[3],[4])))\nprint(apply(coords,[4],[4])[:20], len(apply(coords,[4],[4])))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
