 get the outward ray direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/22/code.py:47:#      the only legal marker geometry and the perpendicular stripe direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/22/code.py:170:    perpendicular to the fixed TL-BR marker diagonal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/22/code.py:346:    Key insight: Once every L-pair uses the same TL-BR anchor diagonal, the solver no longer needs to infer direction per object; that fixed diagonal also determines the stripe geometry, so the only job is to find the bbox and repaint the whole rectangle with perpendicular anti-diagonal bands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/29/code.py:302:                    assert perp, f\"boundary endpoint ({r},{c}) color {color} not perpendicular\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/18/code.py:10:#     moves. Here P must first turn 90 degrees toward the nearer perpendicular border, creating the intended\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/18/code.py:17:#     two perpendicular borders. Generation rejects tied-distance cases.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/18/code.py:34:#     sprouts a perpendicular arm from the nearby endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/18/code.py:46:#   - That pivot turns toward a unique nearer perpendicular boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/18/code.py:312:                        assert perp, f\"boundary endpoint ({r},{c}) color {color} not perpendicular\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/18/code.py:355:    - Execute yellow controls before red-gap repair: each yellow marker identifies a visible endpoint, keeps the arm that reaches that pivot, and turns the line 90 degrees toward the nearer perpendicular boundary. The yellow cell itself stays absent in the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/18/code.py:522:    # Extend non-boundary endpoints to nearest edge (perpendicular to primary axis)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/25/code.py:50:#      Invalid here; internal endpoints are expected, so all boundary/perpendicularity asserts\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/26/code.py:444:                        assert perp, f\"boundary endpoint ({r},{c}) color {color} not perpendicular\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/4/code.py:185:      perpendicular diagonal and paint exactly `2 * L` cells in the segment's color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/5/code.py:333:    - For every outer segment, find the diagonal direction perpendicular to the segment and pointing away from its diamond.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/27/code.py:28:#   from the first visible line, and gap filling relied on axis/perpendicular\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/27/code.py:509:                        assert perp, f\"boundary endpoint ({r},{c}) color {color} not perpendicular\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/27/code.py:588:    - Fill aligned same-color gaps whenever two consecutive cells in a row or column face each other with a bounded gap; no axis-support or perpendicular-support check is applied.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D2/2/code.py:66:  forward scan over other container boxes whose perpendicular spans overlap the mover.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D2/2/code.py:69:  generator therefore keeps blocker containers' own head/dest markers perpendicular to the mover,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D2/2/code.py:80:  unambiguous, and the blocker's own head/destination are placed on a perpendicular side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D2/2/code.py:103:  the perpendicular axis. The generator enforces this explicitly by making blockers fully orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/8/code.py:238:    Key insight: The solver must fuse two independent clues. Marker color n