rpendicular offset\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/13/code.py:30:    The provided baseline code would instead copy the segment at the median perpendicular offset.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/23/code.py:27:#    median perpendicular offset. This combo keeps that target, but the input now hides each logical\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/23/code.py:48:#      so solver now extracts runs first and merges by (color, perpendicular offset).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/23/code.py:81:#      perpendicular offset; generate_input() constructs exactly two runs per track.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/23/code.py:82:#    - main() assumes merged segments have odd count and unique perpendicular offsets; generator keeps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/23/code.py:215:    - Several parallel horizontal, vertical, or diagonal tracks appear at distinct perpendicular offsets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/23/code.py:220:    - Select the logical segment at the median perpendicular offset as the reference span.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/31/code.py:36:  - the channel geometry is now a straight main ray plus one or two perpendicular side branches,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/22/code.py:15:#      16x16 background, with an odd count so one segment is the median by perpendicular offset.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/22/code.py:17:#      perpendicular coordinate is simply the row index.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/22/code.py:39:#    - Original reference selection used perpendicular-dot coordinates. Under horizontal-only inputs,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D16/0/code.py:79:      - perpendicular gap to the axis is 1-2 bg cells, which the solver uses as the local ownership test\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D16/0/code.py:96:      and within a small perpendicular gap from the line\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/6/code.py:12:#   one same-color nub attached one perpendicular step away from one endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/6/code.py:23:#   form: same color, one cell perpendicular from an endpoint, with one common endpoint-side choice\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/6/code.py:246:      body carries one same-color nub attached perpendicular to one endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/6/code.py:250:    - Choose the reference as the segment on the median perpendicular offset.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/30/code.py:54:#    Distinct perpendicular offsets keep the anti-diagonals separated. The dash pattern reduces clutter, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/30/code.py:238:    - Parse every colored object as a dashed anti-diagonal segment and order the segments by perpendicular\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/14/code.py:39:#    perpendicular offsets and the original gap rules keep segments non-overlapping even when colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/14/code.py:158:    - Use the segment at the median perpendicular offset as the reference, taking its terminal endpoint and length.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D4/3/code.py:11:#       - L source: 2 equal-length teal rays, required to be perpendicular\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D4/3/code.py:77:#       - L sources use perpendicular rays rather than opposite rays\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D4/3/code.py:161:    - The source is either a T (3 equal arms) or an L (2 perpendicular equal arms).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/12/code.py:42:#    perpendicular offsets with gaps >= 4, ensuring no overlap between parallel lines. The input is derived by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/12/code.py:178:    - Choose the segment with the median perpendicular offset as the reference.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D5/1/code.py:338:    \"\"\"Coordinate perpendicular to direction d (column for vertical, row for horizontal).\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D5/1/code.py:348:    \"\"\"Sort coordinates by their perpendicular value relative to direction d.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D5/2/code.py:294:    \"\"\"Coordinate perpendicular to direction d (column for vertical, row for horizontal).\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D5/2/code.py:304:    \"\"\"Sort coordinates by their perpendicular value relative to direction d.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D9/2/code.py:85:    \"\"\"Coordinate perpendicular to direction d (column for vertical, row for horizontal).\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D9/2/code.py:95:    \"\"\"Sort coordinates by their perpendicular value relative to direction d.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/291dc1e1/D4/1/code.py:8:#   direction perpendicular to the blue edge. In canonical view that means rows\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D19/2/code.py:121:    \"\"\"Sort coordinates by their perpendicular value relative to direction d.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D19/2/code.py:157:    - When a blob is hit, split its blue body across the axis perpendicular to its green-port direction: the port-facing half turns red, the opposite half stays blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D19/2/code.py:327:    \"\"\"Coordinate perpendicular to direction d (column for vertical, row for horizontal).\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D2/1/code.py:316:    \"\"\"Coordinate perpendicular to direction d (column for vertical, row for horizontal).\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D2/1/code.py:326:    \"\"\"Sort coordinates by their perpendicular value relative to direction d.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/2