offsets\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D7/2/code.py:168:    - Use the segment at the median perpendicular offset as the reference, then shift all segments so their starts match it and redraw them at the reference length.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b0039139/D4/3/code.py:23:#      original, perpendicular-axis mirror, original, perpendicular-axis mirror, ...\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D1/1/code.py:15:       old provided code would ignore those lengths and pick the middle row by perpendicular order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D1/1/code.py:35:   - The old code assumed the reference could be identified from the sorted perpendicular offsets. That\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D1/1/code.py:44:   - Because each segment stays on its own perpendicular line and the gaps remain >=2 for orthogonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D1/1/code.py:267:    \"\"\"Return list of (r, c) for a segment starting at t0 with given perpendicular offset s, or None if any cell is OOB.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D1/1/code.py:279:    \"\"\"Max segment length extending forward from t0 at perpendicular offset s.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D1/1/code.py:288:    \"\"\"Max segment length extending backward from t1 at perpendicular offset s.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D1/1/code.py:297:    \"\"\"Valid range (lo, hi) inclusive for perpendicular offset s given direction d.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D1/1/code.py:308:    \"\"\"Enumerate all valid perpendicular gap sequences of length n-1, ensuring irregular spacing.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D1/1/code.py:323:    \"\"\"Pick n distinct perpendicular offsets with irregular gaps.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D14/2/code.py:42:#    segments on distinct parallel lines. Because lines never share a perpendicular offset,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/