e chosen from perpendicular-order statistics, so it needed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/0/code.py:43:#    The solver still assumes one unique dominant direction, one segment per perpendicular offset, an\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/0/code.py:130:    - Use the segment at the median perpendicular offset as the reference, taking its start position and length.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/0/code.py:15:#    - They still share one dominant direction and have distinct perpendicular offsets with visible gaps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/0/code.py:59:#      unique perpendicular offsets, and enough spacing for diagonal disambiguation. The generator keeps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/0/code.py:107:    - Use the segment at the median perpendicular offset as the reference line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/0/code.py:259:    \"\"\"Max segment length extending forward from t0 at perpendicular offset s.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/0/code.py:268:    \"\"\"Max segment length extending backward from t1 at perpendicular offset s.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/0/code.py:277:    \"\"\"Valid range (lo, hi) inclusive for perpendicular offset s given direction d.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/0/code.py:288:    \"\"\"Enumerate all valid perpendicular gap sequences of length n-1, ensuring irregular spacing.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/0/code.py:303:    \"\"\"Pick n distinct perpendicular offsets with irregular gaps.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/1/code.py:26:#    distinct perpendicular offsets. The reference is still the segment at the median offset.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/1/code.py:46:#    Output segments all start at the same t0 but can have mixed lengths. Because perpendicular\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/1/code.py:101:    - Those segments can be shorter than, equal to, or longer than the middle segment selected by perpendicular position.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/1/code.py:105:    - Use the segment at the median perpendicular offset as the reference, then shift every segment so its start matches the reference start.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/1/code.py:38:#   - Median-by-perpendicular-offset still works because offsets remain unique and the count is odd.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/1/code.py:47:#   - Distinct perpendicular offsets prevent overlap even when colors repeat.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/1/code.py:104:    - Pick the segment at the median perpendicular offset as the reference.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/1/code.py:247:    \"\"\"Return list of (r, c) for a segment starting at t0 with given perpendicular offset s, or None if any cell is OOB.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/1/code.py:259:    \"\"\"Max segment length extending forward from t0 at perpendicular offset s.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/1/code.py:268:    \"\"\"Max segment length extending backward from t1 at perpendicular offset s.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/1/code.py:277:    \"\"\"Valid range (lo, hi) inclusive for perpendicular offset s given direction d.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/1/code.py:288:    \"\"\"Enumerate all valid perpendicular gap sequences of length n-1, ensuring irregular spacing.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/1/code.py:303:    \"\"\"Pick n distinct perpendicular offsets with irregular gaps.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/3/code.py:35:#     Keep 3 or 5 segments, a single shared direction, unique perpendicular\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/3/code.py:65:#     Unique perpendicular offsets prevent any overlap between segments or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/3/code.py:149:    - Detect the common direction and choose the segment at the median perpendicular offset as the reference.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/3/code.py:309:    \"\"\"Return list of (r, c) for a segment starting at t0 with given perpendicular offset s, or None if any cell is OOB.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/3/code.py:321:    \"\"\"Max segment length extending forward from t0 at perpendicular offset s.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/3/code.py:330:    \"\"\"Max segment length extending backward from t1 at perpendicular offset s.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/3/code.py:339:    \"\"\"Valid range (lo, hi) inclusive for perpendicular offset s given direction d.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/3/code.py:350:    \"\"\"Enumerate all valid perpendicular gap sequences of length n-1, ensuring irregular spacing.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/3/code.py:365:    \"\"\"Pick n distinct perpendicular offsets with irregular gaps.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/2/code.py:8:#   placed exactly one perpendicular step away from the segment's center cell. This extra center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/2/code.py:30:#   The generator keeps the original odd segment count, unique perpendicular offsets, and dominant\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/2/code.py:38:#   one consistent perpendicular side per puzzle to avoid clutter.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/2/code.py:194:      one-cell nub attached perpendicular to its center cell, using the same color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/2/code.py:201:    - Choose the reference segment as the one at the median perpendicular offset.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D3/2/code.py:204:      center on the same perpendicular side as before.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/2/code.py:115:    - Detect the shared direction and choose the segment at the median perpendicular offset as the reference.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/2/code.py:260:    \"\"\"Return list of (r, c) for a segment starting at t0 with given perpendicular offset s, or None if any cell is OOB.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/2/code.py:272:    \"\"\"Max segment length extending forward from t0 at perpendicular offset s.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/2/code.py:281:    \"\"\"Max segment length extending backward from t1 at perpendicular offset s.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/2/code.py:290:    \"\"\"Valid range (lo, hi) inclusive for perpendicular offset s given direction d.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/2/code.py:301:    \"\"\"Enumerate all valid perpendicular gap sequences of length n-1, ensuring irregular spacing.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e376de54/D4/2/code.py:316:    \"\"\"Pick n distinct perpendicular offsets with irregular gaps.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4a21e3da/D5/0/code.py:278:    # Force two perpendicular controls so the recolor branch is always observable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4a21e3da/D5/2/code.py:77:#       Generator still places 1 or 2 perpendicular ctrl pixels only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4a21e3da/D5/4/code.py:242:    # Force two perpendicular controls so the D5 difference is always visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4a21e3da/D9/0/code.py:54:#     - region seeds are built on the split-adjacent boundary plus short outward arms, guaranteeing connectivity,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D4/2/code.py:53:#   neighbor and one perpendicular target-color neighbor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D2/0/code.py:249:    - Red/blue obstacle bars (2/1) are thin floating segments perpendicular to the path direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D2/3/code.py:21:     border. The generator therefore keeps bars perpendicular to travel and keeps blue-count encoding,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D2/3/code.py:208:    - Each bar is a 1-cell-thick segment perpendicular to the travel direction; blue cells remain embedded in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4a21e3da/D3/3/code.py:43:- When two arrows exist, they remain perpendicular exactly as in the original task:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4a21e3da/D17/0/code.py:14:#     one or two border control pixels on perpendicular edges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b0280bc/D3/0/code.py:278:    - use_diagonal: diagonal distance-1 when both perpendicular cells are empty.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b0280bc/D6/0/code.py:258:    - use_diagonal: diagonal distance-1 when both perpendicular cells are empty.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b0280bc/D6/1/code.py:333:    - use_diagonal: diagonal distance-1 when both perpendicular cells are empty.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
